Open a session's menu by swiping its sidebar row to the left on touch devices.

On phones and tablets a long press on a session row both picked the row up
for dragging and, a moment later, opened its menu, so the row jumped around
under the menu. Now a long press only picks the row up, and swiping a row
from right to left reveals a "more" button that opens the same menu as the
desktop kebab and right-click. Only horizontal swipes count; scrolling the
list is unchanged. One row is open at a time, and a tap, a scroll or a drag
closes it. Touch devices are those with no hover and a coarse pointer, so
mouse and trackpad devices keep their menus as they were at any width. Also
stops a long press released without moving from loading the session as a
new page.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0005.

